      {
        "id": "p2-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Expand $(x-1)(1+x+x^2)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3-1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)(1+x+x^2)&=x+x^2+x^3-1-x-x^2\\\\(x-1)(1+x+x^2)&=x^3-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p2-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Deduce that $1+x+x^2=\\frac{x^3-1}{x-1}$, for $x\\ne 1$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Divide both sides of $(x-1)(1+x+x^2)=x^3-1$ by $x-1$, which is nonzero for $x\\ne 1$.",
          "worked": "From part (a), $(x-1)(1+x+x^2)=x^3-1$. Since $x\\ne 1$, divide by $x-1$ to obtain\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^3-1}{x-1}&=\\frac{(x-1)(1+x+x^2)}{x-1}\\\\\\frac{x^3-1}{x-1}&=1+x+x^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
